WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.578
<v Human Services Supervisor>Thanks for coming in. I want to ask you about

00:00:02.578 --> 00:00:05.156
<v Human Services Supervisor>the county workgroup. You mentioned last month that you had

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:07.734
<v Human Services Supervisor>been hoping for partner work. What made you bring it

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:07.992
<v Human Services Supervisor>up?

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.342
<v Human Services Specialist>Honestly, I had watched the same two people lead three

00:00:11.342 --> 00:00:14.342
<v Human Services Specialist>groups in a row. I did not think anyone was

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:17.342
<v Human Services Specialist>being unfair. I just could not see how anyone else

00:00:17.342 --> 00:00:17.942
<v Human Services Specialist>got in.

00:00:18.292 --> 00:00:21.216
<v Human Services Supervisor>That is fair. I looked back at the year after

00:00:21.216 --> 00:00:24.139
<v Human Services Supervisor>you said that. You were right about the pattern. Each

00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:27.063
<v Human Services Supervisor>choice felt reasonable at the time, but together they told

00:00:27.063 --> 00:00:27.940
<v Human Services Supervisor>a different story.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.065
<v Human Services Specialist>What changed this time? You did not just ask for

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:32.442
<v Human Services Specialist>volunteers.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:36.272
<v Human Services Supervisor>I wrote the requirements before I thought about names. Know

00:00:36.272 --> 00:00:39.752
<v Human Services Supervisor>the waiver rules, explain them clearly to county staff, manage

00:00:39.752 --> 00:00:43.232
<v Human Services Supervisor>a timeline. Then I added one more: someone who has

00:00:43.232 --> 00:00:46.712
<v Human Services Supervisor>not led with partners yet. Research shows people bend the

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:50.192
<v Human Services Supervisor>criteria to fit whoever they already have in mind. Writing

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:52.280
<v Human Services Supervisor>them first is the simplest guard.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.978
<v Human Services Specialist>I noticed you asked me directly. If you had sent

00:00:55.978 --> 00:00:59.326
<v Human Services Specialist>an email, I probably would have offered to take notes.

00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:02.978
<v Human Services Supervisor>That is exactly what the studies on quiet tasks found.

00:01:02.978 --> 00:01:06.280
<v Human Services Supervisor>People are asked based on who they expect will say

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.252
<v Human Services Supervisor>yes. So notes now rotate for everyone, including me.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.859
<v Human Services Specialist>I was nervous about the timeline. Pairing me with the

00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:16.116
<v Human Services Specialist>consultant for the first month helped. But I am glad

00:01:16.116 --> 00:01:18.722
<v Human Services Specialist>she advised and did not run the meetings.

00:01:19.072 --> 00:01:21.789
<v Human Services Supervisor>That was deliberate. If she had run the meetings, you

00:01:21.789 --> 00:01:24.507
<v Human Services Supervisor>would have learned by watching and nobody would have seen

00:01:24.507 --> 00:01:27.224
<v Human Services Supervisor>your work. The point was for you to build a

00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:27.496
<v Human Services Supervisor>record.

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:30.894
<v Human Services Specialist>Can I ask what happens with the leadership presentation?

00:01:31.244 --> 00:01:33.950
<v Human Services Supervisor>You present it. And when the division manager asks me

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.656
<v Human Services Supervisor>who is ready for more, I plan to say your

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:39.363
<v Human Services Supervisor>name and point to this work. A mentor gives advice.

00:01:39.363 --> 00:01:42.069
<v Human Services Supervisor>A sponsor speaks for you where the decision is made.

00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:44.775
<v Human Services Supervisor>I want to do both, and for more people than

00:01:44.775 --> 00:01:46.940
<v Human Services Supervisor>the two I used to think of first.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.273
<v Human Services Specialist>Then I will make sure the presentation gives you something

00:01:50.273 --> 00:01:51.466
<v Human Services Specialist>specific to point to.
